1
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:29,027
‎Once clear of the Boomboom family,
‎the damage mostly wore off.

2
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:31,781
‎I might not be fully healed though.

3
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:34,325
‎What kind of trick is that?

4
00:00:34,909 --> 00:00:39,288
‎Rather than a trick, it might be better
‎to think of it as a curse.

5
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,290
‎A curse?

6
00:00:40,999 --> 00:00:42,791
‎It seems that once they touch you,

7
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:47,254
‎getting caught between the three of them
‎triggers a powerful attack.

8
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:49,673
‎A curse that pulls iron.

9
00:00:49,674 --> 00:00:51,468
‎Like magnets pulling together.

10
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,305
‎It's late, but we have no choice.

11
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:59,142
‎We have to keep moving
‎so they don't catch up.

12
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:05,439
‎Gyro! Someone's coming after us!

13
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,066
‎It's the Boomboom family.

14
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:10,235
‎The magnetic pull will start again
‎if they get too close!

15
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:12,322
‎Don't let them catch up to us.

16
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:23,958
‎Johnny Joestar is the killer
‎of three competitors.

17
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:27,212
‎And given the situation…

18
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:30,048
‎I'll arrest him and put an end to this.

19
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:31,758
‎Dead or alive!

20
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:57,784
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

21
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:18,239
‎#04
‎THE DEVIL'S PALM

22
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:28,457
‎Damn! He hasn't
‎slowed down one bit, has he?

23
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:31,960
‎Even though both his horse and ours
‎should be at their limit.

24
00:03:31,961 --> 00:03:33,962
‎Something's off.

25
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:36,381
‎Is that really the Boomboom family?

26
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:40,011
‎That strange hat…
‎I feel like I've seen it before.

27
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:44,182
‎Gyro! What's with him?

28
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:47,018
‎He's already over the rise!

29
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:50,521
‎Wait… I know him.

30
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:52,648
‎It's Mountain Tim!

31
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:55,652
‎Why is he chasing us?

32
00:03:56,611 --> 00:04:00,782
‎Good. They're almost
‎within magnetic range.

33
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:07,663
‎Those three magnets
‎will have no choice but to stick together.

34
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:11,376
‎Then they'll tear themselves apart
‎and spill their guts, right?

35
00:04:33,856 --> 00:04:36,984
‎Damn! We've been running nonstop.

36
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:38,568
‎He's still speeding up.

37
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:39,821
‎That's insane!

38
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,365
‎No. Gyro.

39
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:47,161
‎I'm starting to understand.
‎That's not what's going on.

40
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:51,958
‎He is speeding up. But that's not all!

41
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:57,046
‎I'm being pulled backward!

42
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:01,551
‎Johnny!

43
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:09,391
‎Yes! He fell off his horse.
‎That settles it!

44
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:10,475
‎Awesome!

45
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:12,561
‎Way to go, Mountain Tim!

46
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:16,482
‎All that's left is for the three magnets
‎to stick together!

47
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,901
‎Dad, let's go watch!

48
00:05:19,902 --> 00:05:25,574
‎I want to see them tear themselves apart
‎and spill their guts up close!

49
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:26,576
‎Yeah!

50
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:38,795
‎Hey, Dad… I feel cold.

51
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:41,506
‎My vision's blurry and I'm so cold.

52
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:44,593
‎I think something's really wrong with me.

53
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:49,264
‎Cold? We've got bigger things
‎to worry about, Andrew.

54
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:52,018
‎Is that really what matters right now?

55
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:04,404
‎I've somehow become a human magnet too!

56
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:08,325
‎Johnny. When did they touch you?

57
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:10,494
‎You must've been touched somewhere!

58
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:12,580
‎I have no idea.

59
00:06:13,122 --> 00:06:15,624
‎Maybe it was the bullet.

60
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:18,960
‎The bullet Benny Boomboom fired…

61
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:21,379
‎Maybe it had something on it!

62
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:24,382
‎Damn it! We've got to find them.

63
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:26,134
‎Where are they?

64
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:29,263
‎They've got to be nearby
‎controlling this magnetism.

65
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:37,938
‎Maybe they've already done their part.

66
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:41,775
‎Mountain Tim… I don't know
‎why he's after us,

67
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:44,153
‎but this started when he got close to us.

68
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:55,205
‎Hey, Johnny. What are you doing?

69
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:57,874
‎I'm being dragged backward.

70
00:06:57,875 --> 00:06:59,293
‎You're being pulled too, Gyro!

71
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:12,556
‎It's Mountain Tim! He must've been touched
‎by them somewhere too!

72
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:17,186
‎The three of us have been pulling
‎each other without realizing it!

73
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:21,022
‎With only two of us,
‎it was probably too weak to notice.

74
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:24,651
‎But when all three of us got close,
‎we all started pulling one another.

75
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:28,489
‎The magnetic force combined
‎and reached its maximum!

76
00:07:29,615 --> 00:07:32,660
‎We're pulled backward while he speeds up!

77
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:37,414
‎How is he still on his horse?

78
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:41,293
‎He doesn't realize it
‎because he's riding straight toward us!

79
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:43,546
‎What happens if he reaches us?

80
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:49,093
‎My skin… The iron in my blood
‎is being drawn together.

81
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,013
‎Don't let him get any closer!

82
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:57,184
‎If he gets any closer,
‎all three of us will burst apart!

83
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:59,687
‎We've got to warn him
‎to get off his horse!

84
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:04,941
‎What? Why is Johnny Joestar off his horse?

85
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:09,112
‎Gyro Zeppeli's there too.
‎They're shouting something.

86
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:12,200
‎Stop! Stay back!

87
00:08:12,825 --> 00:08:15,952
‎No! He can't hear us!
‎He's coming straight at us!

88
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:20,790
‎Even if he could hear us,
‎I doubt he'd just get off his horse.

89
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:25,087
‎If we don't tell him he's been magnetized,
‎all three of us will die!

90
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:29,550
‎Right. Then let's get him off his horse!

91
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:36,097
‎No, Gyro! It won't reach him!

92
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:40,060
‎The Steel Ball will come right back
‎to your magnetized body!

93
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:42,062
‎I know, Johnny.

94
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:46,692
‎The magnetism will pull the Steel Ball
‎back to me, right?

95
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:50,696
‎That's the part I'm counting on.

96
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:55,159
‎It's enough to pull him off his horse.

97
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:58,662
‎I scattered the rubble.

98
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:00,664
‎But it's gonna hurt bad…

99
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:05,001
‎All three of us.
‎Because we're all magnetic now.

100
00:09:05,002 --> 00:09:07,963
‎There's iron in the rock.

101
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:10,091
‎Cover yourself, Johnny!

102
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:18,391
‎What the…

103
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:23,228
‎We did it!
‎We pulled Mountain Tim off his horse!

104
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:25,939
‎What's this force pulling me in?

105
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:28,818
‎My gun's being pulled onto my arm!

106
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:35,198
‎No, Gyro… We got too close.

107
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:38,660
‎We'd already gotten too close!

108
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:40,955
‎He's flying right at us!

109
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:46,752
‎My blood vessels are bursting!

110
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:49,547
‎Lasso Blues!

111
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:58,514
‎What the hell is that?

112
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:02,309
‎I threw my rope.

113
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:05,605
‎I can move my body in pieces
‎as far as the rope reaches.

114
00:10:06,355 --> 00:10:11,401
‎Looks like if we get any closer,
‎something bad will happen.

115
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:12,485
‎Shit!

116
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:14,571
‎What's wrong, Dad?

117
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:18,284
‎They're gonna get away!
‎We've got to cut that rope!

118
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:24,749
‎I guess I was chasing the wrong man,
‎Johnny Joestar.

119
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:30,463
‎This magnetic force pulling me…
‎Whose ability is it?

120
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:34,884
‎Explain it to me. What's happening?

121
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:40,221
‎LASSO BLUES
‎MOUNTAIN TIM

122
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:41,057
‎TOMB OF THE NOISE 123
‎THE BOOMBOOM FAMILY

123
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:45,393
‎I see. The culprits
‎are the Boomboom family.

124
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:47,646
‎They have the ability to manipulate iron.

125
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:50,941
‎So if I approach you
‎without knowing, I'll die.

126
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:53,109
‎I'll move further away.

127
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:55,362
‎Just what are you?

128
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,990
‎The Boomboom family's one thing,
‎but you too.

129
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:01,452
‎Are you even human? What's going on?

130
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:05,789
‎What about you?
‎What's with that steel ball?

131
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:08,083
‎Mine's just a technique.

132
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:10,419
‎There's still a lot
‎we don't know about humans.

133
00:11:12,296 --> 00:11:16,008
‎I see. There's still much
‎we don't know about humans.

134
00:11:17,426 --> 00:11:20,346
‎I'll keep it brief. It was 15 years ago.

135
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:24,432
‎Back in 1875,

136
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:28,019
‎I was 16 and had joined the military.

137
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:33,317
‎We were assigned to explore
‎an uncharted area of this Arizona desert.

138
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:37,612
‎But my cavalry troop got lost,

139
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:40,491
‎wandering for days in search of water.

140
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:49,125
‎The area was feared by local tribes
‎who called it the "Devil's Palm."

141
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,836
‎We walked right into it.

142
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:56,172
‎Compasses didn't work at all there.

143
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:59,051
‎Quicksand kept the ground
‎constantly shifting.

144
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,469
‎And that wasn't all.

145
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:05,098
‎Entire mountains vanished,
‎valleys appeared,

146
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:07,392
‎and the terrain kept changing.

147
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:09,395
‎That's how we lost our way.

148
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:14,233
‎They say the Devil's Palm
‎moves several miles a day.

149
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:19,237
‎No one knows how large it is
‎or where it is.

150
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:21,323
‎According to the local tribes' legend,

151
00:12:22,032 --> 00:12:25,785
‎a falling star destroyed everything
‎long ago.

152
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:27,913
‎The whole area was left cursed.

153
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:32,585
‎We never found water.

154
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:44,221
‎It was also a place
‎where one could reshape fate.

155
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:53,564
‎For some reason, I woke up.

156
00:12:54,565 --> 00:12:55,941
‎It was late at night.

157
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:02,156
‎A small amount of dew formed on my rope.

158
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:06,744
‎My body soaked it up.

159
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:08,662
‎Unconsciously…

160
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,958
‎my body had become one with the rope.

161
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:16,170
‎I was the only one left alive.

162
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:19,548
‎Perhaps because of some kind of force,

163
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:25,054
‎the Devil's Palm draws out
‎a person's dormant potential.

164
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,766
‎The Indigenous people
‎call it a cursed power.

165
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:31,267
‎Maybe they're right.

166
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:35,064
‎After all, I was supposed to die
‎with everyone else.

167
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:41,861
‎I personally call this ability "Stand."

168
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:44,155
‎One who stands against.

169
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:47,742
‎"Stand… One who stands against"?

170
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,327
‎No doubt about it.

171
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:52,247
‎The Boomboom family
‎must've entered the Devil's Palm

172
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:53,748
‎and gained a Stand.

173
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:55,333
‎So that means

174
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:58,670
‎the only way to keep moving

175
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:01,381
‎is to find them and take them down.

176
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:03,968
‎Nah. I don't think you need to.

177
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:10,306
‎No need to look for us.
‎No need to stay apart, either.

178
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:13,936
‎The only way you can move
‎is closer together.

179
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,689
‎Right, Dad?

180
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:20,483
‎Dad told me so.

181
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:23,945
‎Need a hand, Laurence?
‎Can you cut the rope yourself?

182
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:26,739
‎Mountain Tim's rope, I mean.

183
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:31,078
‎Well… Maybe I can. Maybe I can't.

184
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:45,884
‎Is this made of iron sand?

185
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:48,469
‎He's gathering iron sand and shaping it!

186
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:51,307
‎It's sticking to me. It's so heavy!

187
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:56,270
‎It's charging straight toward
‎Mountain Tim too!

188
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:06,780
‎I knew it. You're too reckless
‎on your own, Laurence!

189
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:10,950
‎Seal up their hands with iron filings too.

190
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:14,954
‎Oh, Dad! I'm so happy!

191
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:19,167
‎Happy? Yeah, we sure are!

192
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,336
‎Don't let them do a thing.

193
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:24,089
‎-Cut Mountain Tim's rope now!
‎-Okay.

194
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,053
‎The rope's been cut!

195
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,221
‎We're done for!

196
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:36,810
‎So heavy…

197
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:39,771
‎It's useless.

198
00:15:39,772 --> 00:15:44,485
‎There's nothing you can do
‎in this magnetic field!

199
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:47,612
‎Johnny. Your hands are free.

200
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:49,698
‎You're the one who has to do it!

201
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,283
‎The Spin, Johnny.

202
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:55,244
‎Use the Spin to take them out.

203
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:57,205
‎There's a bullet right there!

204
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,706
‎Grab it!

205
00:15:58,707 --> 00:16:03,753
‎The bullet's made of lead. It'll fly true
‎even in this magnetic field!

206
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:06,506
‎Spin that bullet!

207
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:07,800
‎Me?

208
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:14,263
‎Johnny, you have to do it!
‎It's Lesson Three!

209
00:16:14,264 --> 00:16:17,142
‎You told me you spun that cork!

210
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:21,187
‎That was a fluke!

211
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:23,064
‎Trust the Spin.

212
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:26,068
‎The Spin holds infinite power. Trust it!

213
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:29,863
‎No! He's coming!

214
00:16:32,282 --> 00:16:34,325
‎They've merged!

215
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,911
‎How far will their guts fly?

216
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:39,372
‎Think they'll break the record?

217
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:40,623
‎We're tearing apart!

218
00:16:40,624 --> 00:16:44,211
‎Johnny! Do it! You have to!

219
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:49,591
‎Can I really do it?
‎I've only made it spin once.

220
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:53,845
‎But this is why I entered this race.

221
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,889
‎To learn the secret of the Spin.

222
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:59,727
‎To master the Spin!

223
00:17:00,602 --> 00:17:04,063
‎Our bodies are gonna burst. Johnny!

224
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:07,192
‎Do it! Or it'll all end here!

225
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:16,452
‎It's spinning… It's spinning, Gyro!

226
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,543
‎Laurence. Don't let your guard down.

227
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:28,797
‎Watch out for
‎a dying man's last-ditch effort.

228
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:32,718
‎No, Gyro… I couldn't make it.

229
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:34,970
‎I failed!

230
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:39,308
‎No… That's not it, Dad.

231
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:42,895
‎Dad, it's not "Watch out."

232
00:17:44,521 --> 00:17:47,523
‎Get back, Dad! Get away from there now!

233
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:49,610
‎What's with his hand?

234
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:55,031
‎Johnny Joestar…

235
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:56,909
‎What's that?

236
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,706
‎My hand…

237
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:07,251
‎My nails… What is this? Gyro!

238
00:18:07,252 --> 00:18:10,963
‎What's going on?
‎The Steel Ball's Spin doesn't do that!

239
00:18:10,964 --> 00:18:13,174
‎Could this be…

240
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:15,802
‎I'm telling you, Dad! Get back!

241
00:18:15,803 --> 00:18:18,430
‎Hurry! Your leg!

242
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:31,235
‎Dad!

243
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:37,406
‎What the hell is happening?

244
00:18:37,407 --> 00:18:39,617
‎Gyro! What was that?

245
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:42,913
‎I haven't got a clue.

246
00:18:43,622 --> 00:18:47,125
‎You bastard! Look what you did to my dad!

247
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,418
‎Johnny!

248
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:52,881
‎Burst your blood vessels and drop dead!

249
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:03,015
‎Impossible! My body…

250
00:19:03,016 --> 00:19:04,977
‎My legs… They leaped!

251
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,563
‎No… No way!

252
00:19:10,941 --> 00:19:15,903
‎Gyro, tell me!
‎What's happening to my fingers?

253
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:19,198
‎That's not the Steel Ball's Spin.

254
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:21,492
‎It's not any technique I know.

255
00:19:21,493 --> 00:19:24,620
‎If it's more than a technique…

256
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:27,166
‎No doubt about it. It's a Stand!

257
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:32,378
‎Johnny Joestar, you've been affected

258
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:34,255
‎by the Devil's Palm.

259
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:37,967
‎I think we're standing in it right now.

260
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:40,595
‎We wandered into it without realizing it.

261
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:44,557
‎A Stand? Me?

262
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:47,102
‎Maybe it was just coincidence.

263
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:50,397
‎Or maybe the land itself pulled us in.

264
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:53,984
‎Probably the latter.

265
00:20:03,493 --> 00:20:04,952
‎Call your horses!

266
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:07,371
‎The terrain's changing.

267
00:20:07,372 --> 00:20:09,583
‎Move, or we'll get lost!

268
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:11,876
‎What? Valkyrie!

269
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:14,795
‎Wait, you bastards!

270
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:17,381
‎I'll never forgive you!

271
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:19,884
‎I'll make you pay.

272
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:22,554
‎I've still got my brother!

273
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:26,642
‎Andrew! Take them down!

274
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:32,813
‎Andrew!

275
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:36,443
‎Forget about them.
‎The Boomboom family is finished.

276
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:39,445
‎Maybe so.

277
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:41,822
‎Gyro Zeppeli!

278
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:45,660
‎You'll never make it to the finish anyway!

279
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:49,790
‎You think we're the only ones
‎after your life?

280
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:56,837
‎We went after you

281
00:20:56,838 --> 00:21:01,384
‎because someone promised us
‎200,000 dollars if you died!

282
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:05,347
‎You've got a bounty on your head.

283
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:08,850
‎Who hired you guys?

284
00:21:09,851 --> 00:21:11,895
‎What are you doing? Move!

285
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:16,649
‎Don't waste time! We'll lose our bearings!

286
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:21,237
‎Get back here! Come back!

287
00:21:21,238 --> 00:21:23,448
‎I'll kill you!

288
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:27,159
‎Dad…

289
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:29,788
‎Andrew…

290
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:46,263
‎The change that occurred in me…
‎Just what was that?

291
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:48,849
‎But more importantly…

292
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,226
‎Who is Gyro, really?

293
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:53,353
‎Is he a wanted man?

294
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:55,856
‎Just what is he hiding?

295
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:35,956
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
